nd an after-after-party  muumuu dress the scene ends with poppy  shouting I want to wear them all the  scene was cut as although it's very  entertaining the filmmakers felt it was  too long and during test screenings at  DreamWorks some people thought it made  poppy seem spoiled and obnoxious by the  way if you've seen my video on the  deleted characters and rejected concepts  in trolls you'll know that in one of the  movies trailers when the villainous chef  raids the troll village poppy is dressed  in what looks like a ceremonial gown  however in the final film the same scene  shows poppy wearing her normal clothes  that's because the party  puppy was having at that point in the  film was originally going to be her  coronation party rather than just a  celebration party which it was in the  final film there was a deleted song  called bringing back happy that I was  really disappointed didn't make it into  the final movie it was going to be a  villain song for the Bergen chef where  we'd see her get deliciously bad as she  sings about how she's bringing back  happiness by cooking up the trolls that  she's captured it's a fantastic musical  number sung by Christine Baranski who  voiced chef in the movie and we get to  see some of her villainous plans to  mince up the trolls whip them into a  batter and chop them into sushi there's  a touch of Hollywood's golden age of  musicals including Carmen Miranda Esther  Williams and choreographer Busby  Berkeley to the song and dance routine  and I just love it it's such a shame it  didn't make it into the final movie as  villains songs in animations can be so  memorable for example I love Ursula's  poor unfortunate souls and the Little  Mermaid and more recently Tama Toa  SHINee in Moana however the filmmakers  didn't include the song because they  thought it made the Bergen villain too  appealing and not frightening enough now  what do you think about the deleted  scenes and song and would you like to  seen them in the movi